   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend a chapter of the laws of 2021, amending the real property law\nrelating to requiring real estate brokers and salespersons to receive implicit\nbias training as part of their license renewal process, as proposed in\nlegislative bills numbers S. 538-B and A. 4638-A, in relation to the\neffectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S7769",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7769-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap of 2021 (as proposed in S.538-A & A.4638-A)",
    "lawSection": "Real Property",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7769\n\nSPONSOR: KAPLAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend a chapter of the laws of 2021, amending the real proper-\nty law relating to requiring real estate brokers and salespersons to\nreceive implicit bias training as part of their license renewal process,\nas proposed in legislative bills numbers S. 538-B and A. 4638-A, in\nrelation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that changes the effective date of L.2021,\nc.686.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the effective date of the underlying chapter\nfrom 180 days after enactment to nine months after enactment.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 686 of the Laws of 2021. S.538-B passed the\nSenate in February 2021, and A.4638-A passed the Assembly in June 2021.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
